problem_statement:
Granted as a whole to roles, databases are not shown in SHOW DATABASES

If a role is granted on the whole database ({{SELECT ON db.* TO role1;}}), and a user is granted this role ({{GRANT role1 TO user1;}}), then that databases is not listed by {{SHOW DATABASES;}}, but still can be used (set as default, {{SHOW TABLES IN ...}}, {{DESCRIBE ...}})


Test case:

{noformat}
--error 0,ER_CANNOT_USER
drop user beep@'%';

--error 0,ER_CANNOT_USER
drop role r1;

drop database if exists db;

create role r1;
create user beep@'%';

create database db;
create table db.t1 (i int);
grant select on db.* to r1;
grant r1 to beep@'%';

--connect (con1,localhost,beep,,)
show databases;
set role r1;
show databases;
{noformat}

Expected result (hopefully):
{noformat}
drop user beep@'%';
drop role r1;
drop database if exists db;
Warnings:
Note	1008	Can't drop database 'db'; database doesn't exist
create role r1;
create user beep@'%';
create database db;
create table db.t1 (i int);
grant select on db.* to r1;
grant r1 to beep@'%';
show databases;
Database
information_schema
test
set role r1;
show databases;
Database
db
information_schema
test
{noformat}

Failing:
{noformat}
@@ -16,6 +16,5 @@
 set role r1;
 show databases;
 Database
-db
 information_schema
 test

mysqltest: Result length mismatch
{noformat}
